{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: kernel K2, K3 and K11 at exact head 6c15e85f2a76af89fb9d1e995e47aa3206e9a577, tree 3160c521762b965cda0b4aa36ee04749102c0c32 (review request 64553b7e, promise 86d62e72, implementation 30c7c3ec / 79ee2bae). This head is the sole child of 51d24df8, which I reviewed in 07f5b878 with two documentation findings, F1 and F2. Both are fixed. Everything else in that review carries over unchanged, because no code, test, seal or evidence byte differs. The head satisfies request 30c7c3ec under structural ruling 9ed512c0, and its evidence meets planner ruling 88630b3c for this head. It may land. Deployment is planner-owned.\n\nRead order: I read the primary, notes/implementation/2026-10-24-kernel-hygiene.md (artifact 3eadf551), first and in full. Then I read the diff from 51d24df8.\n\nWhat changed. git diff 51d24df8..6c15e85f changes exactly one path, docs/kernel.md. Under docs/testing.md:597, no new gate is needed.\n\nF1 fixed. docs/kernel.md no longer says \"pending\" anywhere. The introduction, section 5, the K2 and K11 items, the K11 table row and the section 7 maintained-check paragraph now state results that stay true after landing. They say that the ordinary gate at 8658d109 failed, that the whole-file and previously unreached checks then passed, and that the workroom records the review and landing decisions.\n\nF2 fixed. Section 7 now names the two kernel file and export additions under its own rule, with the reason for each:\n- derive/src/field-types.ts and the ./field-types export: a grammar rule beside the validator that already used and re-exported it;\n- the type-only Signer export from bytes/src/signer.ts: the signature domain that bytes already owns, previously exposed through bytes/application.\nI agree with both reasons. Neither part can be a platform service, and neither adds a new kernel capability.\n\nThe four conditions of ruling 88630b3c hold.\n1. 6c15e85f differs from 51d24df8 only in docs/kernel.md. Outside notes/, 51d24df8 differs from the gated 8658d109 only in examples/lending/vitest.config.ts.\n2. The raw stages/test.log of gate 306f0211 (result.json SHA-256 08b9339f) reads \"Test Files 4 failed | 489 passed | 1 skipped (494)\". The four failed files are browser/custody.test.ts and browser/model.test.ts (not loaded: ENOTDIR), archive-git-v2-layout.test.ts and floor-archive.test.ts. Every stage before the tests exited 0. Node 39 and Counting 55 did not run.\n3. Receipts 0a5dd2b0, 3e2711cd and fb719719 record runs at 59e64247 (tree 2a6c32d2), each with a natural exit 0, the original limits and no retry:\n   - whole Lending, 18 cases in 5 files;\n   - Node 39 and Counting 55;\n   - whole floor-archive, 4 cases;\n   - whole replay layout, 1 case.\n4. The note keeps gate 306f0211 as failed, and says load or process pressure \"is an inference; the exact cause remains unproved\".\nI also note the planner's open point: if either archive test fails again in any gate, the raw output goes to the planner.\n\nDocument checks at 6c15e85f:\n- git diff --check against 51d24df8 is clean;\n- check-commit-messages from e63b2a7b reports 6 checked, 0 flagged;\n- section citations, run on an export, report 1,877 resolved, 0 broken and 5 known unresolved;\n- `node scripts/check-kernel-boundary.mjs` reports 124 production sources and 0 refusals.\n\nCarried from 07f5b878, citing docs/kernel.md section 7:\n- Moves only: every moved codec, validator and test file differs from Main e63b2a7b only in import specifiers. No live importer of an old path remains.\n- Placement: production derive no longer imports package-graph (K2); bytes holds no application codec (K3); examples/demo-repo and its guide references are removed (K11).\n- The boundary check refused both of my uncommitted controls: a platform import from derive, and a package-graph import from bytes, each naming its file.\n- The gate and continuation account, which the ruling's conditions cover:\n  - the raw gate at 8658d109 shows 3,509 passed, 3 skipped and 2 failed (the replay and floor cases), plus two Lending files that did not load (9 cases absent);\n  - the repaired tree 2a6c32d2 changes only the two Lending aliases;\n  - whole Lending (18), floor (4), replay (1), Node 39 and Counting 55 all passed at 2a6c32d2;\n  - this head adds only notes and docs/kernel.md.\n  The original gate stays failed. The load explanation for the floor and replay failures is an inference.\n\nArchitecture: unchanged from 07f5b878. The kernel is contract, bytes and derive, with three pinned libraries. Codecs and package validation are in platform. One maintained boundary check runs before Vitest in npm test.\nSecurity: unchanged from 07f5b878; I found no defect. No authority, route, gate class or runtime check changes. The seven seal values change only because their import specifiers change. The documentation adds no secret.\nSimplification: unchanged. The documentation change only adds the requested statements. The plain-string dap-derive alias in apps/counter/vitest.config.ts:10 remains a nonblocking note.\n\nFindings: none open. No deployment or publication is claimed or approved here.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3eadf551c276b9f190288c36528f1f1b2f5dd649","binding":"assigned","head":"6c15e85f2a76af89fb9d1e995e47aa3206e9a577","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:86d62e72fb85e9120f5eab81af68314e2f59113e\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:88630b3c4ad1f13142940d9b4587be01d8991e55\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:79ee2bae4fbe94426d0ac3d916af9f1b248fad8b\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a5b8546928928e3aa20b3ed17850d911be8719bf","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}